IMPORT prelude
IMPORT types

-- Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ)
-- Schedule 1 -- Transitional, savings, and related provisions (cl 9).
-- Source: registers/source-bundle/LMS1592864.xml, 2026 No 339-1, retrieved 2026-09-11.
--
-- Three clauses. Sch 1 cl 1 defines the commencement date; Sch 1 cl 2 applies
-- cl 11 to accounts created before commencement; Sch 1 cl 3 substitutes a
-- 6-month deadline for cl 15(1)(a) in the case of operators trading at the start
-- of the commencement date. The asymmetry between the two is #19.

§ `Schedule 1 -- Provisions relating to this Act as enacted`

§§ `Periods`

-- cl 2 of the Act: commencement is 6 months after Royal assent.
-- Sch 1 cl 3(2): existing operators then have a further 6 months to file.
-- cl 15(1)(a): everyone else has 12 months from the date the platform meets
-- the definition of age-restricted platform.

`months from Royal assent to commencement`                           MEANS  6
`months after commencement for an existing operator to file`         MEANS  6
`months after qualifying for any other operator to file`             MEANS 12

§§ `1. Interpretation`

-- Sch 1 cl 1: commencement date means the date on which this Act comes into
-- force. Modelled as a fact about an account or an operator rather than as a
-- date, because nothing in the Schedule computes from a calendar date.

§§ `2. Section 11 applies in respect of accounts created before, on, and after commencement date`

DECLARE `account` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    `the account holder is a New Zealand person under 16 years`                          IS A BOOLEAN
    `the account was created before the commencement date`                               IS A BOOLEAN
    `the platform is an age-restricted platform`                                          IS A BOOLEAN

-- Sch 1 cl 2: cl 11 applies regardless of when the account was created. The
-- creation date is therefore carried in the record and then not consulted,
-- which is the point: no arm of the rule turns on it.

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) Sch 1 cl 2
@export Decide whether the clause 11 duty applies in respect of an account
GIVEN a IS A `account` @desc The account: whether the holder is a New Zealand person under 16, whether the account was created before the commencement date, and whether the platform is an age-restricted platform.
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the section 11 duty applies in respect of the account` IF
        a's `the platform is an age-restricted platform`
    AND a's `the account holder is a New Zealand person under 16 years`

§§ `3. Existing operators must provide child safety risk assessment within 6 months`

DECLARE `transitional filing` HAS
    name                                                                                IS A STRING
    -- Sch 1 cl 3(1)
    `the person was an operator of an age-restricted platform at the start of commencement` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- the cl 15(1)(a) trigger for everyone else
    `the platform met the definition of age-restricted platform after commencement`      IS A BOOLEAN

-- Sch 1 cl 3(2): for an operator trading at the start of the commencement date,
-- cl 15 is to be read as requiring provision within 6 months after commencement.
-- For any other operator cl 15(1)(a) applies unmodified: 12 months from the date
-- the platform met the definition.

@ref Online Safety (Minimum Age and Child Safety Risk Assessment) Bill (NZ) Sch 1 cl 3
@export Compute the number of months an operator has to provide its first child safety risk assessment
GIVEN f IS A `transitional filing` @desc Whether the person was already an operator of an age-restricted platform at the start of the commencement date, or the platform met the definition only afterwards.
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `months to provide the first risk assessment for` f IS
    IF   f's `the person was an operator of an age-restricted platform at the start of commencement`
    THEN `months after commencement for an existing operator to file`
    ELSE `months after qualifying for any other operator to file`

§§ `Scenario fixtures`

-- An account opened by a 14-year-old two years before the Act commences.
`a pre-existing under-16 account` MEANS `account` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "account opened in 2024 by a 14-year-old"
    `the account holder is a New Zealand person under 16 years`                          IS TRUE
    `the account was created before the commencement date`                               IS TRUE
    `the platform is an age-restricted platform`                                          IS TRUE

`a new under-16 account` MEANS `account` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "account opened the day after commencement"
    `the account holder is a New Zealand person under 16 years`                          IS TRUE
    `the account was created before the commencement date`                               IS FALSE
    `the platform is an age-restricted platform`                                          IS TRUE

`an operator trading at commencement` MEANS `transitional filing` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "platform already operating on day one"
    `the person was an operator of an age-restricted platform at the start of commencement` IS TRUE
    `the platform met the definition of age-restricted platform after commencement`      IS FALSE

`a platform caught later by regulations` MEANS `transitional filing` WITH
    name                                                                                IS "service specified as a platform under cl 62 a year later"
    `the person was an operator of an age-restricted platform at the start of commencement` IS FALSE
    `the platform met the definition of age-restricted platform after commencement`      IS TRUE

§§ `Machine-evaluated cases`

-- Sch 1 cl 2: the creation date makes no difference. The duty bites on the
-- existing user base from the commencement date itself.
#EVAL `the section 11 duty applies in respect of the account` `a pre-existing under-16 account`
#ASSERT `the section 11 duty applies in respect of the account` `a pre-existing under-16 account` EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `the section 11 duty applies in respect of the account` `a new under-16 account` EQUALS TRUE

-- Sch 1 cl 3(2) against cl 15(1)(a): an operator already trading gets 6 months
-- for the paperwork duty, while a platform caught later by cl 62 regulations
-- gets 12. Neither gets any transitional period at all for the cl 11 duty.
-- See NOTES.md, #19.
#EVAL `months to provide the first risk assessment for` `an operator trading at commencement`
#EVAL `months to provide the first risk assessment for` `a platform caught later by regulations`
#ASSERT `months to provide the first risk assessment for` `an operator trading at commencement` EQUALS 6
#ASSERT `months to provide the first risk assessment for` `a platform caught later by regulations` EQUALS 12
